///1LINK
Help by Willem Aandewiel
LINK - Digital Research LINK-80 linker

///2SYNTAX
  E>A:LINK DEMO
  E>A:LINK MAIN,UTIL

The default input extension is .REL.
The second example normally creates MAIN.COM and MAIN.SYM.

///2ORDER
Place the startup module first, followed by the required modules.
Do not run a resulting program with unresolved symbols.

///2COMPARISON
LINK combines relocatable modules. LOAD processes Intel HEX.
This syntax applies to Digital Research LINK-80.
Microsoft L80 and other linkers use different command forms.
